  "limitations": [
    "Stationary single camera; no general indoor/near-plane/truncation acceptance.",
    "Root triangle projection uses a three-pixel diagnostic guard and full-view fallback for nonpositive/near-zero w; not a formal general floating-point bound.",
    "Envelope readback validates the bounds after timing; it does not produce the policy.",
    "Layer counters measure depth-passing coverage; shader invocations before depth rejection remain unknown.",
    "Split mode keeps logical population and per-pixel ordering but repeats vertex work in five disjoint scissor regions.",
    "CPU mirrors, GL state inspection once per frame, and uniform forwarding remain installed in both variants; CPU/FPS are diagnostic comparisons, not a shipping implementation forecast.",
    "Original split shader removes the predicate call but retains unused portal declarations. Clean split explicitly strips the declarations/helpers and forwards changed uniforms only."
  ]
}
